1
00:00:12,679 --> 00:00:14,681
[grave music]

2
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:19,269
[breath trembling]

3
00:00:24,190 --> 00:00:25,066
Let us go--

4
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,651
[gasps]

5
00:00:35,160 --> 00:00:36,411
Wait, please don't shoot.

6
00:00:38,621 --> 00:00:40,206
I have a sick daughter at home who…

7
00:00:42,917 --> 00:00:43,918
[groans]

8
00:00:50,967 --> 00:00:52,260
[No-eul] Close your eyes.

9
00:00:53,553 --> 00:00:55,221
If you want to live, do as I say.

10
00:01:04,856 --> 00:01:05,857
[scanner beeps]

11
00:01:06,566 --> 00:01:08,818
[woman on PA] Player 246, eliminated.

12
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:21,372
SQUID GAME 3

13
00:01:23,917 --> 00:01:28,338
EPISODE 1
KEYS AND KNIVES

14
00:01:44,229 --> 00:01:45,563
[masked soldier] Take him away.

15
00:01:55,448 --> 00:01:58,243
What's with you playing nice with us
all of a sudden?

16
00:01:58,326 --> 00:01:59,494
It's not like you.

17
00:02:00,453 --> 00:02:01,955
[No-eul] I gave it some more thought.

18
00:02:02,038 --> 00:02:03,706
If they're just gonna die anyway,

19
00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:06,876
might as well give their organs
to people who can still be saved.

20
00:02:06,960 --> 00:02:08,253
[masked soldier chuckles]

21
00:02:09,003 --> 00:02:10,004
Good call.

22
00:02:10,505 --> 00:02:12,674
I'm glad to hear you finally came around.

23
00:02:15,677 --> 00:02:16,803
[No-eul] I wanna see it.

24
00:02:18,721 --> 00:02:20,765
-[masked soldier] See what?
-The operating room.

25
00:02:22,559 --> 00:02:23,977
[masked soldier] What for?

26
00:02:27,564 --> 00:02:30,483
[No-eul] Well, now that we're partners,

27
00:02:31,401 --> 00:02:33,570
there shouldn't be any secrets between us.

28
00:02:36,781 --> 00:02:38,366
[alarm buzzing]

29
00:02:39,951 --> 00:02:41,953
[eerie music]

30
00:03:13,318 --> 00:03:15,320
[players whispering indistinctly]

31
00:03:16,738 --> 00:03:17,739
[door closes]

32
00:03:20,700 --> 00:03:22,869
[man 1] Guess it's someone
who died out there.

33
00:03:24,120 --> 00:03:25,121
[man 2] Who is that?

34
00:03:30,209 --> 00:03:31,377
[gasps]

35
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:32,378
Is he dead?

36
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:35,590
He's alive.

37
00:03:35,673 --> 00:03:38,051
-Come here. Help me get him to a bed.
-[sighs]

38
00:03:38,134 --> 00:03:39,969
-Quick!
-[Yong-sik] Yeah, of course.

39
00:03:40,053 --> 00:03:42,639
[Geum-ja] Here, just…
Wait, lay him down here.

40
00:03:47,435 --> 00:03:49,437
[mercenary] I don't see him
anywhere near the boat.

41
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:52,357
Do you remember how many drinks he had?

42
00:03:53,524 --> 00:03:54,943
Not enough to get wasted.

43
00:03:55,026 --> 00:03:56,152
Sure looked like a lot

44
00:03:56,236 --> 00:03:58,905
from those soju bottles
on the cabin floor this morning.

45
00:04:00,698 --> 00:04:03,409
He could've gotten drunk,
came out to the deck to throw up,

46
00:04:03,493 --> 00:04:05,119
and ended up falling overboard.

47
00:04:05,745 --> 00:04:07,622
The waves were pretty rough last night.

48
00:04:07,705 --> 00:04:10,917
Oh, you know,
I wonder if that was the sound I heard.

49
00:04:11,668 --> 00:04:12,627
What sound?

50
00:04:12,710 --> 00:04:15,296
Uh, at some point,
someone was talking outside,

51
00:04:15,380 --> 00:04:17,173
then I heard these thumping sounds.

52
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,341
What time was that?

53
00:04:18,424 --> 00:04:20,635
I think it was about 3:00 a.m. Wasn't it?

54
00:04:20,718 --> 00:04:22,178
Yep, that sounds about right.

55
00:04:22,262 --> 00:04:25,515
I got up to check, but Captain Park
was already out on the deck.

56
00:04:25,598 --> 00:04:28,309
[groans] We should've woken everyone up
and looked for him.

57
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,061
We should search the vicinity first.

58
00:04:30,144 --> 00:04:33,189
Listen, Detective,
these are strong currents we got out here.

59
00:04:33,273 --> 00:04:35,733
He would've drifted quite a ways
since last night.

60
00:04:35,817 --> 00:04:38,278
If he was drunk when he fell,
in weather like that, well…

61
00:04:38,361 --> 00:04:40,947
Can you waste time
looking for a corpse? Huh?

62
00:04:41,030 --> 00:04:43,283
You said we had three, four days, at most.

63
00:04:46,119 --> 00:04:48,830
We'll head to the nearest docks
and find another drone pilot.

64
00:04:50,957 --> 00:04:51,791
Let's move out.

65
00:04:58,840 --> 00:05:00,842
[ominous music]

66
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:15,857
[In-ho] We have to attack first.

67
00:05:15,940 --> 00:05:17,984
[Gi-hun] Doesn't mean we should join
this bloodbath.

68
00:05:18,067 --> 00:05:19,777
We'd be playing into their hands
if we did.

69
00:05:19,861 --> 00:05:21,529
[In-ho] Sacrifice a few for the rest?

70
00:05:21,612 --> 00:05:23,281
[Gi-hun] And it'll be worth the sacrifice

71
00:05:23,364 --> 00:05:25,491
if it means we can put an end
to these games for good.

72
00:05:25,575 --> 00:05:27,785
[Jung-bae] If they won't let us go
we fight our way out.

73
00:05:27,869 --> 00:05:30,204
[Gi-hun] If you wanna take out
these fuckers, step forward.

74
00:05:30,288 --> 00:05:32,040
[Jung-bae]
Why take me instead of Young-il?

75
00:05:32,123 --> 00:05:33,666
[Gi-hun] 'Cause you're my best friend.

76
00:05:36,377 --> 00:05:37,795
[Geum-ja shakily] Mr. Seong.

77
00:05:38,338 --> 00:05:40,340
[tense music]

78
00:05:41,424 --> 00:05:43,509
Oh, you… Oh, goodness, you're awake.

79
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:44,594
You're alive.

80
00:05:45,219 --> 00:05:46,554
[laughing] You're alive.

81
00:05:47,305 --> 00:05:48,806
Are you feeling better, sir?

82
00:06:11,996 --> 00:06:13,998
[players murmuring]

83
00:06:16,793 --> 00:06:18,377
[man] It's suspicious, right?

84
00:06:18,461 --> 00:06:20,463
[murmuring continues]

85
00:06:22,465 --> 00:06:24,050
Where's… where's everyone else?

86
00:06:33,059 --> 00:06:34,769
And Jung-bae, did he…

87
00:06:37,438 --> 00:06:39,690
[sinister music]

88
00:06:45,113 --> 00:06:49,742
[Front Man] Now, witness the consequences
of your little game.

89
00:06:49,826 --> 00:06:50,743
[Jung-bae] Gi-hun…

90
00:06:51,661 --> 00:06:52,662
[gunshot]

91
00:06:55,414 --> 00:06:57,416
[dark music]

92
00:07:00,128 --> 00:07:02,130
[breath trembling]

93
00:07:02,213 --> 00:07:03,965
[alarm buzzing]

94
00:07:10,429 --> 00:07:11,889
-[door closes]
-[remote beeps]

95
00:07:11,973 --> 00:07:12,974
[ceiling rumbles]

96
00:07:14,308 --> 00:07:16,394
[digital trilling]

97
00:07:18,563 --> 00:07:21,983
[masked manager] Last night,
another 35 players were eliminated,

98
00:07:22,066 --> 00:07:24,777
bringing the current number
of remaining players to 60.

99
00:07:25,611 --> 00:07:28,656
The total prize is now 39.6 billion won,

100
00:07:28,739 --> 00:07:31,868
and each player's share
is 660 million won.

101
00:07:33,494 --> 00:07:35,371
We will now begin another round of voting

102
00:07:35,455 --> 00:07:38,291
to determine if you wish to proceed
to the next game.

103
00:07:39,000 --> 00:07:41,085
[footsteps approaching]

104
00:07:42,670 --> 00:07:44,755
Why'd you let me live, and no one else?

105
00:07:44,839 --> 00:07:46,299
Why didn't you kill me?

106
00:07:46,924 --> 00:07:48,259
Answer me!

107
00:07:48,342 --> 00:07:49,844
What's it for, huh?

108
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:52,263
You didn't let anyone else live. Why?!

109
00:07:53,306 --> 00:07:55,558
Here, go ahead.
Shoot. Go ahead, pull the trigger!

110
00:07:55,641 --> 00:07:57,185
Go on, do it!

111
00:07:57,268 --> 00:07:58,769
Kill me. Take the shot!

112
00:08:01,105 --> 00:08:03,357
Why did you let me live? Why?

113
00:08:04,692 --> 00:08:07,153
What else do you bastards want from me?

114
00:08:09,280 --> 00:08:11,741
Why didn't you just kill me
like everyone else?

115
00:08:11,824 --> 00:08:12,825
[sobbing]

116
00:08:14,911 --> 00:08:16,204
You won, didn't you?

117
00:08:17,455 --> 00:08:20,416
Go ahead, just take the fucking shot!

118
00:08:22,668 --> 00:08:25,004
You beat us! You won!

119
00:08:27,798 --> 00:08:31,886
-So please, I'm begging you, just kill me!
-[phone ringing]

120
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:36,599
[screams] Kill me!

121
00:08:41,646 --> 00:08:43,481
We just docked at the nearest port.

122
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:47,318
They're gonna find another drone pilot
and head out again.

123
00:08:47,818 --> 00:08:49,320
They must not find the island.

124
00:08:49,403 --> 00:08:51,572
Not till we're done
with all the games here.

125
00:08:51,656 --> 00:08:52,657
[Captain] Understood.

126
00:08:54,325 --> 00:08:55,701
Hey, Detective Hwang!

127
00:08:55,785 --> 00:08:57,870
Gimme a call
once you're ready to head back out!

128
00:08:58,913 --> 00:09:01,499
-Will do.
-[Captain] And, uh, watch your step there.

129
00:09:05,670 --> 00:09:08,714
Last question.
What do I do if things go south?

130
00:09:15,471 --> 00:09:16,472
Kill them all.

131
00:09:17,723 --> 00:09:19,100
Including the detective.

132
00:09:21,185 --> 00:09:23,104
[somber music]

133
00:09:23,187 --> 00:09:25,481
[masked manager]
We will now begin another round of voting

134
00:09:25,565 --> 00:09:28,234
to determine if you wish to proceed
to the next game.

135
00:09:29,360 --> 00:09:33,239
Once again, it will be conducted
in reverse player-number order.

136
00:09:33,322 --> 00:09:35,825
Player 456, please cast your vote.

137
00:09:44,709 --> 00:09:47,420
If you do not express an intent to vote
by the count of three,

138
00:09:47,503 --> 00:09:49,338
it will be considered an abstention.

139
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:54,885
One, two, three.

140
00:09:57,972 --> 00:09:59,807
Player 456 has forfeited his vote,

141
00:09:59,890 --> 00:10:03,227
and as such,
his will not be added to either tally.

142
00:10:03,311 --> 00:10:06,355
Next, Player 448. Please cast your vote.

143
00:10:24,040 --> 00:10:26,042
[man 1] Don't worry, you can relax.

144
00:10:26,125 --> 00:10:27,835
We're not gonna hurt you, okay?

145
00:10:28,836 --> 00:10:30,630
[man 2] Yeah, you can vote for either one!

146
00:10:30,713 --> 00:10:32,548
[man 3]
Don't worry about anyone else, okay?

147
00:10:32,632 --> 00:10:34,133
Just vote however you want!

148
00:10:36,260 --> 00:10:37,094
[beeps]

149
00:10:39,055 --> 00:10:41,307
-[excited whispering]
-[man 4] First one's with us.

150
00:10:56,864 --> 00:10:58,741
[elevator door closes]

151
00:10:58,824 --> 00:11:00,785
[Masked Officer]
So far, the confirmed casualties

152
00:11:00,868 --> 00:11:03,371
are 8 managers and 27 soldiers.

153
00:11:04,246 --> 00:11:06,874
[Front Man] Pull from the workers
to replace the dead soldiers.

154
00:11:06,957 --> 00:11:10,211
And repair any damage to the facility
as quickly as possible.

155
00:11:10,961 --> 00:11:12,672
The VIPs will be arriving soon.

156
00:11:12,755 --> 00:11:13,839
[Masked Officer] Yes, sir.

157
00:11:13,923 --> 00:11:15,925
[ominous music]

158
00:11:23,432 --> 00:11:25,434
[forklift beeping]

159
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:43,994
[loud thud]

160
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,841
[masked soldier]
Where'd you learn how to shoot?

161
00:11:56,924 --> 00:11:57,967
Oh, wait.

162
00:11:58,050 --> 00:12:01,762
I heard North Korean women have to serve
in the military too. You learn there?

163
00:12:02,263 --> 00:12:03,389
[No-eul] That's right.

164
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:06,267
[masked soldier]
So then why'd you cross the border?

165
00:12:06,767 --> 00:12:08,394
Were things pretty bad up there?

166
00:12:09,019 --> 00:12:10,229
Or maybe

167
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:13,315
you landed yourself in some hot water.

168
00:12:15,776 --> 00:12:16,902
[masked soldier sighs]

169
00:12:17,695 --> 00:12:19,655
You said we were partners now.

170
00:12:19,738 --> 00:12:22,241
So shouldn't we get to know
each other a bit?

171
00:12:22,324 --> 00:12:25,327
[No-eul] We can meet on the outside
once this is all over.

172
00:12:25,411 --> 00:12:26,787
I'll tell you everything then.

173
00:12:26,871 --> 00:12:28,330
[masked soldier sighs]

174
00:12:28,414 --> 00:12:29,874
I don't wanna wait till then.

175
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:32,918
You know,
there's a great place for a date nearby.

176
00:12:33,002 --> 00:12:34,128
Wanna check it out?

177
00:12:34,211 --> 00:12:35,671
[No-eul] It's a long story.

178
00:12:36,255 --> 00:12:37,840
Let me see the operating room first.

179
00:12:37,923 --> 00:12:39,091
[masked soldier] Sure.

180
00:12:39,800 --> 00:12:42,011
I've had my eye on this spot for a while.

181
00:12:42,094 --> 00:12:43,220
You're gonna love it.

182
00:12:43,888 --> 00:12:45,014
[laughs]

183
00:12:49,268 --> 00:12:51,145
[masked manager]
In accordance with the results

184
00:12:51,228 --> 00:12:52,688
of your free and democratic vote,

185
00:12:52,771 --> 00:12:55,274
we will proceed
with the next game tomorrow.

186
00:12:55,858 --> 00:12:56,859
Thank you all.

187
00:13:01,906 --> 00:13:04,033
-[alarm buzzing]
-[door opens]

188
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:06,869
[indistinct conversations]

189
00:13:10,414 --> 00:13:11,415
[door closes]

190
00:13:15,211 --> 00:13:16,587
[Jeong-dae] Hey, 456.

191
00:13:17,963 --> 00:13:19,006
Tell me something.

192
00:13:19,632 --> 00:13:21,759
Was this part of your plan the whole time?

193
00:13:22,468 --> 00:13:24,053
Oh, that's it, isn't it?

194
00:13:24,136 --> 00:13:26,472
You get everyone
to join your little rebellion

195
00:13:26,555 --> 00:13:28,641
so you could get rid of them all at once.

196
00:13:29,225 --> 00:13:31,685
[snaps fingers]
Ah, so that means that earlier…

197
00:13:31,769 --> 00:13:34,813
-[screaming] …"Why didn't I die?!"
-[players laugh]

198
00:13:34,897 --> 00:13:36,357
All that shit was an act.

199
00:13:36,857 --> 00:13:39,276
Wow. Talk about a twisted freak.

200
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:40,778
I bet you're right.

201
00:13:40,861 --> 00:13:42,988
'Cause after all,
those assholes killed everyone

202
00:13:43,072 --> 00:13:44,657
but decided to spare him.

203
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:46,450
There's a reason for that, isn't there?

204
00:13:46,534 --> 00:13:49,745
Well, in any case, you brought those
dumbass Xs out there to die,

205
00:13:49,828 --> 00:13:51,747
so now they're out of our way.

206
00:13:51,830 --> 00:13:55,334
You got us a larger share,
and helped us win today's vote.

207
00:13:55,417 --> 00:13:56,377
Thanks for that.

208
00:13:56,919 --> 00:13:59,713
Now, let's show our man some gratitude
with a round of applause!

209
00:13:59,797 --> 00:14:01,757
-[cheering, whooping]
-[man 1] Good job!

210
00:14:01,840 --> 00:14:03,592
[man 2] Couldn't have done it without ya!

211
00:14:03,676 --> 00:14:05,844
[man 3] You've been on our side all along!

212
00:14:09,890 --> 00:14:11,392
[Seon-nyeo] Oh, you poor fool.

213
00:14:12,059 --> 00:14:13,519
What did I tell you?

214
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:16,855
You're not here of your own volition,
are you?

215
00:14:16,939 --> 00:14:19,149
It was the vengeful souls
hovering over you

216
00:14:19,233 --> 00:14:20,568
that dragged you here.

217
00:14:20,651 --> 00:14:22,653
[eerie music]

218
00:14:29,785 --> 00:14:31,120
Do you hear that?

219
00:14:31,203 --> 00:14:35,416
It's the sound of all your little friends,
screaming into your ears from the dead.

220
00:14:37,042 --> 00:14:39,044
Ah, but cover them all you want.

221
00:14:40,004 --> 00:14:41,547
It won't stop the noise.

222
00:14:42,256 --> 00:14:44,508
You'll only hear them
scream louder each day.

223
00:14:45,259 --> 00:14:46,218
And you…

224
00:14:46,302 --> 00:14:50,180
You're going to continue to hear them
from now until the day that you die.

225
00:14:51,140 --> 00:14:52,600
[laughing]

226
00:14:59,732 --> 00:15:01,191
[Seon-nyeo gasps]

227
00:15:01,275 --> 00:15:03,611
[Player 006] Let her go!
Stop it! Let her go.

228
00:15:03,694 --> 00:15:04,528
[Gi-hun strains]

229
00:15:07,323 --> 00:15:08,157
[Gi-hun grunts]

230
00:15:10,284 --> 00:15:12,453
[Player 006]
Are you all right, Miss Seon-nyeo?

231
00:15:12,536 --> 00:15:14,538
[Seon-nyeo breathing heavily]

232
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:17,583
[handcuffs rattling]

233
00:15:19,835 --> 00:15:21,837
[ominous music]

234
00:15:40,606 --> 00:15:41,649
How's this one?

235
00:15:42,232 --> 00:15:43,859
We'll be able to get some good stuff.

236
00:15:43,943 --> 00:15:45,945
[eerie music]

237
00:15:49,239 --> 00:15:50,658
[man 1] Okay, nice and easy.

238
00:15:51,742 --> 00:15:53,410
-One, two, three!
-[man 2] Three!

239
00:15:55,412 --> 00:15:56,372
[door opens]

240
00:15:58,374 --> 00:16:00,376
[man 3] It's okay. You guys can relax.

241
00:16:02,670 --> 00:16:04,463
Number 011's on our side now.

242
00:16:06,256 --> 00:16:07,925
Your friend there's in good shape, right?

243
00:16:09,426 --> 00:16:12,012
That was all her.
It's a little present for us.

244
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:14,431
Why'd you bring her all the way down here?

245
00:16:16,934 --> 00:16:18,644
We're all partners now, okay?

246
00:16:19,478 --> 00:16:21,355
We should get to know each other a little.

247
00:16:23,148 --> 00:16:24,900
The guys here before us

248
00:16:25,818 --> 00:16:28,737
only wound up getting caught
'cause they wanted to keep secrets.

249
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:30,155
There was no trust.

250
00:16:30,239 --> 00:16:32,825
But we trust each other.
We have no secrets.

251
00:16:33,492 --> 00:16:36,453
That's why we agreed
not to wear our masks in here.

252
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:40,040
Isn't it?

253
00:16:41,542 --> 00:16:42,418
[man 1 exhales]

254
00:16:56,390 --> 00:16:57,683
[doctor] So you're Number 011.

255
00:16:58,684 --> 00:17:01,478
You know much money we lost
'cause of the shit you pulled out there?

256
00:17:02,396 --> 00:17:05,065
That's enough.
We gotta hurry if we're gonna make it.

257
00:17:05,149 --> 00:17:06,358
Help me here.

258
00:17:08,736 --> 00:17:09,945
[man 3] Hey, come here.

259
00:17:11,196 --> 00:17:13,365
I'll walk you through
the whole thing, okay?

260
00:17:17,327 --> 00:17:19,246
There's your present on the table now.

261
00:17:19,872 --> 00:17:21,457
He's still alive, right, Doc?

262
00:17:21,540 --> 00:17:23,292
Yeah. Just unconscious.

263
00:17:24,293 --> 00:17:25,294
All right then.

264
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:28,005
Let's all thank Number 011
for the lovely gift.

265
00:17:28,589 --> 00:17:29,715
Time to open it.

266
00:17:29,798 --> 00:17:30,966
[doctor chuckles]

267
00:17:34,261 --> 00:17:36,138
-[groans]
-[tense music]

268
00:17:36,221 --> 00:17:38,057
-Freeze.
-[doctor] What the fuck!

269
00:17:38,140 --> 00:17:39,224
Put the knife down.

270
00:17:39,308 --> 00:17:40,893
-Putting it down!
-What are you doing?

271
00:17:40,976 --> 00:17:42,394
[No-eul] You step back!

272
00:17:42,478 --> 00:17:45,147
-[man 3] I thought you were one of us now.
-[man 1] Goddamn bitch!

273
00:17:47,399 --> 00:17:48,358
[man 3 screams]

274
00:17:54,198 --> 00:17:55,074
Fuck.

275
00:18:00,496 --> 00:18:02,247
[breath trembling]

276
00:18:02,331 --> 00:18:03,540
-[gunshot]
-[man 3 gasps]

277
00:18:06,376 --> 00:18:08,378
[breath trembles]

278
00:18:09,546 --> 00:18:11,715
You wanted to know
why I crossed the border?

279
00:18:14,343 --> 00:18:16,720
I had a commander a lot like you up there.

280
00:18:18,597 --> 00:18:19,765
I shot him in the head.

281
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:22,518
-[chuckles]
-[ominous music]

282
00:18:33,695 --> 00:18:35,781
[breathing heavily] Don't kill me.

283
00:18:36,573 --> 00:18:38,283
I swear, I'm not one of them.

284
00:18:39,201 --> 00:18:41,578
I just got roped into this.
They… they offered me money.

285
00:18:42,204 --> 00:18:43,497
[No-eul] This man…

286
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:44,498
Save him.

287
00:18:46,708 --> 00:18:48,168
If he dies, so do you.

288
00:18:54,466 --> 00:18:56,468
[mysterious music]

289
00:19:41,972 --> 00:19:42,973
[Myung-gi] Jun-hee.

290
00:19:47,644 --> 00:19:49,104
I know they're your favorite.

291
00:20:15,589 --> 00:20:17,174
I don't think that's a good idea.

292
00:20:17,257 --> 00:20:18,926
I'll be fine. You just eat yours.

293
00:20:21,845 --> 00:20:23,096
Um, excuse me, sir.

294
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:27,851
Here, have this. You need to try and eat.

295
00:20:35,525 --> 00:20:36,610
Listen, I know.

296
00:20:37,736 --> 00:20:38,987
You wanted to help us.

297
00:20:39,947 --> 00:20:42,282
You were trying to save
everyone out there.

298
00:20:43,033 --> 00:20:46,828
To teach those bad people a lesson
and end this whole thing.

299
00:20:49,248 --> 00:20:50,249
I'm sorry.

300
00:20:50,332 --> 00:20:52,334
[dark music]

301
00:20:54,294 --> 00:20:55,504
I should've done more…

302
00:20:57,506 --> 00:20:59,132
to bring the ammo back to you.

303
00:21:01,927 --> 00:21:03,720
Hyun-ju, why are you sorry?

304
00:21:04,763 --> 00:21:06,181
This is Dae-ho's fault.

305
00:21:07,266 --> 00:21:09,226
Come on, I saw it, my mom saw it.

306
00:21:09,309 --> 00:21:11,061
Everyone here saw what happened.

307
00:21:12,229 --> 00:21:13,647
As soon as Dae-ho got here,

308
00:21:13,730 --> 00:21:15,774
he took the rounds,
went to leave, and then just

309
00:21:17,150 --> 00:21:19,194
froze and sank right to the floor.

310
00:21:19,278 --> 00:21:22,322
And by the time Hyun-ju got here,
it was already too late.

311
00:21:22,406 --> 00:21:24,533
The guards had all started to rush in.

312
00:21:24,616 --> 00:21:26,827
And if my mom hadn't stopped her,
then, well,

313
00:21:28,537 --> 00:21:30,205
Hyun-ju would've died too.

314
00:21:30,289 --> 00:21:31,665
That's the truth, right?

315
00:21:32,624 --> 00:21:35,711
[Geum-ja] Look, sitting here
won't bring anyone back from the dead.

316
00:21:36,503 --> 00:21:38,171
Let's focus on who's still here.

317
00:21:38,672 --> 00:21:39,673
Right, sir?

318
00:21:42,384 --> 00:21:44,469
Go on. Try to eat a little.

319
00:21:45,053 --> 00:21:48,056
And please drink some water
so you don't choke.

320
00:21:52,686 --> 00:21:54,938
Oh, dear. He's completely out of it.

321
00:22:02,029 --> 00:22:04,031
[eerie music]

322
00:22:21,173 --> 00:22:23,175
NOVEMBER 4 - DAY 4 OF THE SEARCH

323
00:22:31,224 --> 00:22:32,225
[knocking on door]

324
00:22:32,809 --> 00:22:34,770
[Woo-seok] Detective Hwang, you asleep?

325
00:22:35,312 --> 00:22:36,480
Not yet, no.

326
00:22:39,566 --> 00:22:42,069
Listen, uh, if you're still awake,

327
00:22:42,903 --> 00:22:45,322
I thought we could have a chat
over some drinks.

328
00:22:46,782 --> 00:22:47,991
Sure. Come in.

329
00:22:51,119 --> 00:22:52,120
Thanks.

330
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:53,497
Oh, no. None for me.

331
00:22:54,581 --> 00:22:56,333
Uh… Okay.

332
00:23:01,505 --> 00:23:02,547
[Woo-seok exhales]

333
00:23:03,590 --> 00:23:05,675
So, what is it? What's on your mind?

334
00:23:07,594 --> 00:23:08,595
Oh.

335
00:23:10,388 --> 00:23:13,809
It's, um, about Captain Park.

336
00:23:14,935 --> 00:23:16,895
You were saying that
when you almost drowned,

337
00:23:16,978 --> 00:23:19,022
-he's who found you at sea?
-[Jun-ho] Yeah.

338
00:23:19,106 --> 00:23:22,234
I fell into the water
after I got shot on that island.

339
00:23:22,317 --> 00:23:25,112
He's the one who rescued me
and then took me to the hospital.

340
00:23:25,195 --> 00:23:28,198
Well, is there anything else you remember?

341
00:23:28,782 --> 00:23:30,659
No. I woke up in the hospital room.

342
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:32,911
My mother's the one who told me
what he did.

343
00:23:33,995 --> 00:23:34,996
Why?

344
00:23:35,622 --> 00:23:36,832
Uh… [laughs awkwardly]

345
00:23:37,332 --> 00:23:39,084
Uh, it's nothing, just…

346
00:23:39,167 --> 00:23:40,919
Do you remember this morning

347
00:23:41,002 --> 00:23:43,797
I said I went outside last night
'cause of a noise I heard?

348
00:23:43,880 --> 00:23:45,966
Yeah, Captain Park said he heard it too.

349
00:23:46,049 --> 00:23:48,718
Yeah. And I really didn't think
it was strange then.

350
00:23:49,469 --> 00:23:52,722
Only now, looking back at it,
when I saw him,

351
00:23:52,806 --> 00:23:54,516
he was holding something in his hand.

352
00:23:55,183 --> 00:23:56,351
What?

353
00:23:56,434 --> 00:23:57,435
A screwdriver.

354
00:23:58,019 --> 00:23:59,020
[Woo-seok] Who's there?

355
00:23:59,104 --> 00:24:01,398
-[Captain] Ah. Woo-seok!
-[eerie music]

356
00:24:02,899 --> 00:24:04,151
It's just Captain Park!

357
00:24:05,777 --> 00:24:06,778
Screwdriver?

358
00:24:07,654 --> 00:24:08,613
Mmm-hmm.

359
00:24:09,114 --> 00:24:12,951
I know it was dark and all,
but I'm sure he was holding a screwdriver.

360
00:24:13,034 --> 00:24:14,995
That's just a little bit weird, isn't it?

361
00:24:15,078 --> 00:24:17,539
Why would he have something like that
in his hand?

362
00:24:17,622 --> 00:24:19,040
Maybe he was working on the boat.

363
00:24:20,208 --> 00:24:23,628
No, but he said he was in bed
when he heard the strange noise.

364
00:24:23,712 --> 00:24:25,589
What if he wanted a weapon
to defend himself

365
00:24:25,672 --> 00:24:27,215
'cause he felt like something was off?

366
00:24:29,176 --> 00:24:30,177
Well, I guess…

367
00:24:30,719 --> 00:24:32,804
-Uh, it still seems weird for--
-Woo-seok.

368
00:24:33,638 --> 00:24:35,849
You think Captain Park
had something to do with this.

369
00:24:35,932 --> 00:24:37,726
That is what you're saying, isn't it?

370
00:24:41,271 --> 00:24:43,690
Listen, I can always trust my gut,

371
00:24:43,773 --> 00:24:46,735
and it's telling me that there's
something fishy going on with the Captain.

372
00:24:46,818 --> 00:24:48,445
This is the man who saved my life.

373
00:24:49,446 --> 00:24:52,073
Who's spent years
trying to help me track down this island.

374
00:24:52,157 --> 00:24:53,742
And even now, that's what he's doing.

375
00:24:53,825 --> 00:24:55,327
I know that he is.

376
00:24:55,410 --> 00:24:56,786
And look, you know, I'm not saying

377
00:24:56,870 --> 00:24:59,414
he actually did anything
to the drone pilot for sure.

378
00:24:59,497 --> 00:25:00,498
It's only that my gut--

379
00:25:00,582 --> 00:25:02,584
Last night you were with the drone pilot.

380
00:25:02,667 --> 00:25:04,294
You were drinking with him, weren't you?

381
00:25:05,462 --> 00:25:07,130
[hesitating] Oh.

382
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:09,549
Yeah, but not a lot, though.
It was just a few.

383
00:25:10,425 --> 00:25:11,426
[chuckles awkwardly]

384
00:25:12,177 --> 00:25:13,762
We're setting out pretty early.

385
00:25:14,471 --> 00:25:15,972
You should go get some sleep.

386
00:25:18,016 --> 00:25:19,142
Oh.

387
00:25:19,226 --> 00:25:20,310
Sure, okay.

388
00:25:21,937 --> 00:25:23,563
And no more alcohol on the boat.

389
00:25:24,814 --> 00:25:25,941
Starting tomorrow.

390
00:25:30,278 --> 00:25:31,112
Okay.

391
00:25:43,667 --> 00:25:45,669
[eerie music]

392
00:25:47,545 --> 00:25:48,964
[softly] You motherfucker.

393
00:25:50,715 --> 00:25:52,634
They died while you sat around.

394
00:25:55,553 --> 00:25:58,556
[warped classical music playing
on speakers]

395
00:26:20,745 --> 00:26:22,747
[eerie music]

396
00:26:30,672 --> 00:26:32,841
-[alarm buzzing]
-[woman on PA] Your attention, please.

397
00:26:32,924 --> 00:26:35,010
The fourth game will begin momentarily.

398
00:26:35,760 --> 00:26:38,013
Please follow the staff's instructions

399
00:26:38,096 --> 00:26:40,682
and swiftly make your way
towards the game hall.

400
00:26:40,765 --> 00:26:42,767
["The Blue Danube" playing on speakers]

401
00:26:42,851 --> 00:26:43,935
[Masked Officer] Sir.

402
00:26:45,437 --> 00:26:46,896
The VIPs have arrived.

403
00:26:54,321 --> 00:26:56,323
[music intensifies]

404
00:27:10,503 --> 00:27:13,048
[woman on PA]
Players, what you see before you here

405
00:27:13,131 --> 00:27:15,800
is the fate of those
who refused to accept the results

406
00:27:15,884 --> 00:27:18,053
of our free and democratic voting process

407
00:27:18,136 --> 00:27:22,599
by attempting to forcibly put an end
to the games through violent means.

408
00:27:24,017 --> 00:27:25,226
Let us be clear.

409
00:27:25,310 --> 00:27:28,688
We will not tolerate
any further irrational behavior,

410
00:27:28,772 --> 00:27:31,649
-or attempts to violate the fair, just…
-[Dae-ho coughs]

411
00:27:31,733 --> 00:27:34,027
…and clearly outlined rules
of these games.

412
00:27:34,944 --> 00:27:38,698
Such actions will be punished
in accordance with our strict regulations.

413
00:27:38,782 --> 00:27:42,410
We would like to thank you all
for your understanding and cooperation.

414
00:27:43,078 --> 00:27:45,080
[eerie music]

415
00:27:47,999 --> 00:27:50,835
[woman on PA]
Players, welcome to the fourth game.

416
00:27:52,128 --> 00:27:55,632
For this game,
you will be divided into two teams.

417
00:27:56,466 --> 00:27:57,801
Before we can begin,

418
00:27:57,884 --> 00:28:01,137
all players must first receive
their team assignments.

419
00:28:02,263 --> 00:28:04,432
Please step forward one at a time

420
00:28:04,516 --> 00:28:07,394
and draw a ball
from the machine in front of you.

421
00:28:16,403 --> 00:28:18,405
Major internal organs look good.

422
00:28:19,614 --> 00:28:21,199
I was able to stitch him up.

423
00:28:22,325 --> 00:28:24,619
-But?
-He needs a transfusion to live.

424
00:28:25,286 --> 00:28:27,163
And we don't have any blood here.

425
00:28:31,126 --> 00:28:32,168
Use mine then.

426
00:28:32,794 --> 00:28:33,795
What's your type?

427
00:28:33,878 --> 00:28:34,963
Type O.

428
00:28:36,297 --> 00:28:37,507
That should work, right?

429
00:28:38,007 --> 00:28:40,844
-[mechanical clicking]
-[mysterious music]

430
00:28:49,185 --> 00:28:51,187
[mechanical clicking]

431
00:29:18,423 --> 00:29:20,300
[mechanical clicking]

432
00:30:02,217 --> 00:30:05,303
Oh, it's all right.
They haven't even said what we're playing.

433
00:30:19,734 --> 00:30:21,986
-[mechanical clicking]
-[ball clattering]

434
00:30:33,498 --> 00:30:35,500
[dark music]

435
00:30:50,223 --> 00:30:51,933
Try anything, and you're dead.

436
00:31:19,794 --> 00:31:21,754
[masked manager]
The game you'll be playing today

437
00:31:21,838 --> 00:31:23,131
is Hide-and-seek.

438
00:31:23,214 --> 00:31:24,340
[players] Hide-and-seek?

439
00:31:24,424 --> 00:31:26,092
[masked manager] Players on the Blue Team

440
00:31:26,175 --> 00:31:28,344
must either find the exit
and escape within 30 minutes,

441
00:31:28,428 --> 00:31:32,223
or stay hidden to avoid being caught
by members of the Red Team

442
00:31:32,307 --> 00:31:33,766
before the game ends.

443
00:31:33,850 --> 00:31:36,686
Then what do we do?
Is it like the kids' version?

444
00:31:38,730 --> 00:31:40,982
Do we just have to find them
and then they're out?

445
00:31:41,065 --> 00:31:42,317
Players on the Red Team

446
00:31:42,400 --> 00:31:46,237
must find the members of the Blue Team
hiding throughout the arena

447
00:31:46,321 --> 00:31:48,239
and kill them within 30 minutes.

448
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:50,408
-[players gasp, murmur]
-[dark music]

449
00:31:50,491 --> 00:31:51,951
[woman] We have to kill them?

450
00:31:53,119 --> 00:31:55,580
-You did say "kill," right?
-[masked manager] That is correct.

451
00:31:55,663 --> 00:31:59,292
Each player on the Red Team must find
and kill a player on the Blue Team.

452
00:31:59,375 --> 00:32:02,503
If you fail to kill at least one,
you will be eliminated.

453
00:32:02,587 --> 00:32:05,256
So all those people,
they're going to try to kill us?

454
00:32:05,340 --> 00:32:06,215
That is correct.

455
00:32:06,299 --> 00:32:08,843
[players murmuring]

456
00:32:08,927 --> 00:32:10,929
[Yong-sik and Geum-ja breathing shakily]

457
00:32:29,405 --> 00:32:30,239
What's this?

458
00:32:31,157 --> 00:32:33,201
[masked manager]
The item you've been given is a key

459
00:32:33,284 --> 00:32:35,662
that can be used
to unlock doors in the arena.

460
00:32:36,537 --> 00:32:40,750
Using these keys, you will be able
to access new areas during the game.

461
00:32:40,833 --> 00:32:44,629
However, once a door has been opened,
it cannot be locked again.

462
00:32:44,712 --> 00:32:47,298
Whoa, hold on. So those guys
can either hide and wait it out,

463
00:32:47,382 --> 00:32:49,050
or they use their keys to escape?

464
00:32:49,133 --> 00:32:50,677
Sounds like an unfair advantage to me.

465
00:32:50,760 --> 00:32:52,095
-What the fuck!
-Shut the hell up!

466
00:32:52,178 --> 00:32:55,598
It's not just that. You're saying that
we each gotta kill one, right?

467
00:32:56,224 --> 00:32:57,517
And without any tools?

468
00:32:58,101 --> 00:33:00,937
Yeah, it doesn't make any sense at all.

469
00:33:01,020 --> 00:33:04,482
I don't suppose any of them
will just stand there and ask us to do it.

470
00:33:05,400 --> 00:33:07,777
You guys really expect us to do it
with our bare hands?

471
00:33:08,403 --> 00:33:10,029
[masked manager] These points are valid,

472
00:33:10,113 --> 00:33:12,490
and we completely understand
your concerns.

473
00:33:13,074 --> 00:33:17,161
That's why we've gone ahead and prepared
a small gift for the Red Team as well.

474
00:33:17,829 --> 00:33:20,957
Please open your boxes
and inspect their contents.

475
00:33:27,005 --> 00:33:28,006
Thank you, sir.

476
00:33:35,847 --> 00:33:37,765
-[players murmuring]
-[woman 1] Is that a knife?

477
00:33:37,849 --> 00:33:39,142
Whoa, nice.

478
00:33:39,225 --> 00:33:40,893
[woman 2] They've got knives now.

479
00:33:42,353 --> 00:33:44,022
[man 1] What did we get?

480
00:33:44,105 --> 00:33:46,357
-[Nam-gyu] Oh.
-[man 1] What are we to do against knives?

481
00:33:46,441 --> 00:33:48,276
[Nam-gyu exclaims in awe]

482
00:33:49,527 --> 00:33:53,573
[masked manager] You can use these knives
to attack the players on the Blue Team.

483
00:33:54,240 --> 00:33:58,578
But please note, members of the Red Team
are not allowed to attack each other.

484
00:33:58,661 --> 00:34:01,789
Well, shouldn't you at least give us
a shield or something?

485
00:34:01,873 --> 00:34:03,374
They got knives after all.

486
00:34:03,458 --> 00:34:06,377
What are we supposed to do,
run around without any defense?

487
00:34:06,461 --> 00:34:07,462
He's right.

488
00:34:08,046 --> 00:34:10,757
-You need to give us something too.
-I agree.

489
00:34:10,840 --> 00:34:14,302
Look, dude, all we got were these keys.
That's not very fair, is it?

490
00:34:14,385 --> 00:34:15,261
Yeah, he's right.

491
00:34:15,344 --> 00:34:18,556
Those keys open doors, remember?
You people can actually get outta here.

492
00:34:18,639 --> 00:34:21,559
-That's right.
-Or you can just find somewhere to hide.

493
00:34:21,642 --> 00:34:23,436
-You got it easy, man!
-[man 1] Totally!

494
00:34:23,519 --> 00:34:25,855
[man 2] Yeah, it's like a cake walk
for you guys.

495
00:34:25,938 --> 00:34:26,773
Hey, Gramps.

496
00:34:28,649 --> 00:34:30,485
You're good at that kind of thing,
aren't you?

497
00:34:31,569 --> 00:34:33,446
Hiding, like a little rat.

498
00:34:34,030 --> 00:34:35,865
[masked manager]
Before we begin today's game,

499
00:34:35,948 --> 00:34:39,285
we would like to first give you
an opportunity to change your fate.

500
00:34:40,161 --> 00:34:44,373
If any of you are not satisfied
with your currently assigned role,

501
00:34:44,457 --> 00:34:48,127
you may instead choose to switch sides
with someone from the opposing team

502
00:34:48,211 --> 00:34:49,462
before the game begins.

503
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:52,256
-[man 1] What? Change teams?
-[man 2] What? We can switch sides?

504
00:34:52,340 --> 00:34:54,050
[masked manager] That is correct.

505
00:34:54,133 --> 00:34:56,636
-As long as both parties agree…
-[prays indistinctly]

506
00:34:56,719 --> 00:34:59,514
…you may trade your vests and items
with another player.

507
00:35:00,640 --> 00:35:02,934
However, once the game begins,

508
00:35:03,017 --> 00:35:04,352
removing your own vest,

509
00:35:04,435 --> 00:35:06,979
or attempting to switch vests
with any player,

510
00:35:07,063 --> 00:35:08,773
is strictly prohibited.

511
00:35:08,856 --> 00:35:11,901
So please consider carefully
before making your decision.

512
00:35:20,159 --> 00:35:22,787
[man 3] Well, I don't know
which team's got it worse.

513
00:35:22,870 --> 00:35:24,872
-The key's not bad.
-[breath trembling]

514
00:35:35,091 --> 00:35:37,552
All right, guys.
Say hi to the new drone pilot.

515
00:35:37,635 --> 00:35:39,178
[drone operator] Nice to meet you all.

516
00:35:39,262 --> 00:35:41,764
He was hard to find,
so make sure he feels welcome.

517
00:35:41,848 --> 00:35:43,015
[mercenaries] Yes, sir.

518
00:35:44,976 --> 00:35:46,185
[drone operator] Thanks.

519
00:35:46,269 --> 00:35:48,604
-Right then. First things first.
-[eerie music]

520
00:35:48,688 --> 00:35:50,439
-[phone buzzing]
-Go and grab a life jacket.

521
00:35:50,523 --> 00:35:52,275
Don't want any more accidents.

522
00:35:52,358 --> 00:35:54,902
-You heard what happened.
-[drone operator] Ah, yeah.

523
00:35:55,778 --> 00:35:57,613
We're about to head out. Where are you?

524
00:35:57,697 --> 00:36:00,449
[Woo-seok] Detective, you guys go ahead.
I'm not coming.

525
00:36:01,159 --> 00:36:02,827
What do you mean, you're not?

526
00:36:02,910 --> 00:36:05,037
[Woo-seok]
There's just something I gotta look into.

527
00:36:06,831 --> 00:36:08,416
Is this about what you said last night?

528
00:36:09,500 --> 00:36:12,378
I know it sounds weird,
but my gut tends to be right.

529
00:36:12,461 --> 00:36:14,297
I'll be in touch if I find anything.

530
00:36:14,380 --> 00:36:16,340
Until I do, be careful around the Captain.

531
00:36:16,424 --> 00:36:17,258
[Jun-ho] Woo-seok--

532
00:36:19,260 --> 00:36:21,721
[Captain] All right, boys,
it's time to shove off!

533
00:36:22,889 --> 00:36:24,182
-Ready?
-Yeah, all set.

534
00:36:41,616 --> 00:36:44,285
All right, dude, will you explain
what the hell's going on now?

535
00:36:44,368 --> 00:36:47,496
What are you doing here,
and why'd you call me up so early?

536
00:36:47,580 --> 00:36:50,082
I got work now.
I like to sleep in on my days off.

537
00:36:53,336 --> 00:36:54,629
Your old boss is dead.

538
00:36:56,172 --> 00:36:59,342
What? What do you mean, he's dead?
What happened to him?

539
00:37:00,051 --> 00:37:01,552
It's a bit of a long story.

540
00:37:02,970 --> 00:37:04,305
-[sighs]
-I don't…

541
00:37:04,388 --> 00:37:07,391
Why the hell didn't you call me?
Why didn't I know? Huh?

542
00:37:07,975 --> 00:37:10,519
Yeah, I left the crew to go straight,
but still. It's the boss--

543
00:37:10,603 --> 00:37:12,396
No, it's not like that, okay? I…

544
00:37:15,691 --> 00:37:17,985
You know Rock, Paper, Scissors, Minus One?

545
00:37:18,069 --> 00:37:18,945
Yeah, of course.

546
00:37:19,028 --> 00:37:22,114
Okay. Well, so the boss and I
were playing it like this, and…

547
00:37:24,450 --> 00:37:26,869
And he needed to take back one hand.

548
00:37:30,623 --> 00:37:31,624
Anyway…

549
00:37:32,541 --> 00:37:34,710
Uh, let's go get hangover soup
and head out, okay?

550
00:37:34,794 --> 00:37:37,380
Hey, come on, man, what happened then?
Finish the story.

551
00:37:37,463 --> 00:37:40,258
Just start the car.
I'll fill you in on the way.

552
00:37:41,717 --> 00:37:43,928
-I swear, you're being weird, dude.
-[engine starts]

553
00:37:44,011 --> 00:37:47,390
How does someone die playing
Rock, Paper, Scissors, Minus One, huh?

554
00:37:47,473 --> 00:37:49,892
Not a single one of you
will leave here alive,

555
00:37:49,976 --> 00:37:52,812
-not while you walk alone.
-[woman gasps] Then what do we do?

556
00:37:52,895 --> 00:37:56,357
And so instead,
it is I, Seon-nyeo, Shaman of the Sea,

557
00:37:56,983 --> 00:37:59,402
who will guide your way
to find the path of life.

558
00:37:59,485 --> 00:38:01,487
[players praying indistinctly]

559
00:38:03,489 --> 00:38:05,866
I see everything inside this place.

560
00:38:05,950 --> 00:38:08,452
And I can see the way ahead,
all from here.

561
00:38:08,536 --> 00:38:10,162
[players praying indistinctly]

562
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:12,331
[Seon-nyeo] It is not with my eyes I see!

563
00:38:12,415 --> 00:38:16,085
The gods of heaven and earth themselves
have taken my hand.

564
00:38:16,168 --> 00:38:18,921
They're guiding us with their light!

565
00:38:20,548 --> 00:38:22,300
Those who choose to follow me

566
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:25,344
-shall prolong their lives…
-[Nam-gyu] Hey, Min-su.

567
00:38:25,428 --> 00:38:27,513
[Seon-nyeo] And those who stand in my way

568
00:38:27,596 --> 00:38:29,932
-You ever killed anyone?
-[Seon-nyeo] …will fall dead!

569
00:38:31,058 --> 00:38:32,601
[Nam-gyu] Look, there's not much time.

570
00:38:32,685 --> 00:38:35,604
If you can't do this,
you might as well switch teams right now.

571
00:38:35,688 --> 00:38:37,315
I know you're pretty good at hiding.

572
00:38:37,398 --> 00:38:38,816
Ah, Min-su.

573
00:38:38,899 --> 00:38:41,319
I was looking everywhere for you
last night, but

574
00:38:42,069 --> 00:38:43,237
I couldn't find you.

575
00:38:44,613 --> 00:38:45,906
Where'd you run off to?

576
00:38:46,866 --> 00:38:49,660
Dude, you were scared of me, weren't you?

577
00:38:52,830 --> 00:38:53,914
Nice work.

578
00:38:53,998 --> 00:38:56,042
-[withdraws hand]
-You were smart to hide.

579
00:38:56,959 --> 00:38:59,754
And that bitch, dude,
thought she was Wonder Woman.

580
00:38:59,837 --> 00:39:02,631
She always treated me like I was nothing.
What a fucking cunt!

581
00:39:02,715 --> 00:39:04,133
-She got what she…
-[breath shakes]

582
00:39:04,216 --> 00:39:06,218
-[chuckles softly]
-[dark music]

583
00:39:11,932 --> 00:39:12,975
Did you see it?

584
00:39:14,977 --> 00:39:17,104
Oh, you little bastard,
you fucking saw it.

585
00:39:17,188 --> 00:39:20,316
And you just hid there like a baby
and watched her die.

586
00:39:20,399 --> 00:39:21,609
You didn't do anything.

587
00:39:21,692 --> 00:39:24,070
And that bitch
really had a soft spot for you.

588
00:39:25,946 --> 00:39:26,947
Aww!

589
00:39:27,615 --> 00:39:28,616
Poor Min-su.

590
00:39:30,159 --> 00:39:31,869
I just love that look in your eye.

591
00:39:32,953 --> 00:39:35,373
Keep that going
once you get in there, bro.

592
00:39:35,456 --> 00:39:37,416
Then you just gotta take them out.

593
00:39:37,500 --> 00:39:38,501
[knife clatters]

594
00:39:40,836 --> 00:39:43,130
That fucking son of a bitch Thanos
is dead.

595
00:39:43,672 --> 00:39:46,759
And same with our whole crew.
It's just you and me now.

596
00:39:46,842 --> 00:39:49,261
Think how lonely I'll be
if I lose you too.

597
00:39:51,347 --> 00:39:52,473
[breathes heavily]

598
00:39:52,556 --> 00:39:55,518
So I need you to be a man
this time, Min-su. Hmm?

599
00:39:56,227 --> 00:39:57,353
[picks up knife]

600
00:39:57,436 --> 00:39:59,897
[imitating Thanos]
You can do it, my bro, Min-su!

601
00:40:00,564 --> 00:40:01,857
Min-su!

602
00:40:03,192 --> 00:40:06,612
See you soon, Min-su! [laughs]

603
00:40:06,695 --> 00:40:08,531
[Myung-gi] Jun-hee, switch with me.

604
00:40:09,323 --> 00:40:10,449
You take the key.

605
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:12,368
It's our only way out of this.

606
00:40:13,911 --> 00:40:14,995
Leave me alone.

607
00:40:15,538 --> 00:40:16,914
I don't need your charity.

608
00:40:18,457 --> 00:40:20,042
What do you mean, leave you alone?

609
00:40:20,126 --> 00:40:22,545
I know that you won't be able
to hurt anyone with that thing.

610
00:40:22,628 --> 00:40:24,296
You don't know anything about me.

611
00:40:24,380 --> 00:40:26,048
Maybe not, but I do know this…

612
00:40:28,259 --> 00:40:29,427
You're not a murderer.

613
00:40:35,182 --> 00:40:36,350
Here, hand it over.

614
00:40:37,726 --> 00:40:39,937
I'll go in and find someone to take out.

615
00:40:40,938 --> 00:40:42,189
Then I'll come find you.

616
00:40:43,232 --> 00:40:44,400
I'll do what it takes.

617
00:40:45,985 --> 00:40:47,528
For you and our kid.

618
00:40:50,197 --> 00:40:51,907
It's that easy for you to kill someone?

619
00:40:55,035 --> 00:40:56,036
Yes.

620
00:40:57,538 --> 00:41:01,250
I'd do anything for you and the reward,
even if it meant killing everyone.

621
00:41:01,333 --> 00:41:03,419
And I'd do anything to keep my baby safe.

622
00:41:06,297 --> 00:41:07,298
Then…

623
00:41:13,012 --> 00:41:14,430
kill me in there.

624
00:41:17,099 --> 00:41:19,143
I'll come find you once the game starts.

625
00:41:19,894 --> 00:41:21,854
Then you stab me and get out, okay?

626
00:41:27,776 --> 00:41:29,236
You'll both get to live then.

627
00:41:34,783 --> 00:41:35,910
[Yong-sik] Mom,

628
00:41:37,077 --> 00:41:38,412
give me the knife.

629
00:41:41,081 --> 00:41:44,793
Oh, no, I… I can find another player
on your team to switch with.

630
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:48,631
-That way we can stay together and keep--
-Mom, please.

631
00:41:49,215 --> 00:41:50,925
You know how bad your knees are.

632
00:41:53,260 --> 00:41:57,723
As soon as we're in the game room,
then those assholes with their knives

633
00:41:57,806 --> 00:41:59,600
will be on us like a pack of wolves.

634
00:41:59,683 --> 00:42:02,520
If you and I try to stick together
the whole time,

635
00:42:03,646 --> 00:42:05,064
they're gonna hunt us down.

636
00:42:05,856 --> 00:42:07,650
[Geum-ja hesitates, sighs]

637
00:42:07,733 --> 00:42:09,693
Oh, no. I know my son.

638
00:42:11,070 --> 00:42:13,781
Even if you had one of these,
you couldn't kill anyone.

639
00:42:15,574 --> 00:42:17,243
Even when you were a kid,

640
00:42:17,326 --> 00:42:19,662
you'd get in those fights
in the neighborhood,

641
00:42:19,745 --> 00:42:23,332
you'd get so beat up
'cause you'd just stand there.

642
00:42:24,208 --> 00:42:27,336
You've never even thrown a punch,
Yong-sik, let alone killed anyone.

643
00:42:27,419 --> 00:42:28,629
You're no different.

644
00:42:29,755 --> 00:42:32,091
Could you chase someone down
and kill them with that?

645
00:42:32,174 --> 00:42:35,302
Dad beat you all the time,
but you never fought back or anything.

646
00:42:42,685 --> 00:42:43,852
I'll do it.

647
00:42:45,646 --> 00:42:46,647
I…

648
00:42:47,439 --> 00:42:48,524
I will try.

649
00:42:48,607 --> 00:42:51,610
-[both breathe shakily]
-[tense music]

650
00:42:59,535 --> 00:43:01,954
-Thank you.
-[Yeong-sam] Sweet!

651
00:43:04,873 --> 00:43:06,625
Yeah. [chuckles]

652
00:43:07,334 --> 00:43:08,419
Ah, shit.

653
00:43:09,420 --> 00:43:12,339
Much appreciated! [laughs]

654
00:43:13,882 --> 00:43:17,177
I, uh… I was just wondering
if, um, you'd consider switching.

655
00:43:22,850 --> 00:43:24,852
[music intensifies]

656
00:43:28,897 --> 00:43:30,649
[Dae-ho] Just hear me out, please.

657
00:43:30,733 --> 00:43:33,444
Look, if you switch with me,
I can stay right with you,

658
00:43:33,527 --> 00:43:35,404
and make sure you're safe. Huh?

659
00:43:37,448 --> 00:43:39,533
You'd still need to kill another player.

660
00:43:39,617 --> 00:43:40,701
Jesus! Just…

661
00:43:41,243 --> 00:43:43,370
Look. Just… just listen.

662
00:43:44,038 --> 00:43:45,914
I'll handle that, don't worry.

663
00:43:45,998 --> 00:43:47,958
I'll still keep you safe, I swear.

664
00:43:48,542 --> 00:43:50,210
-[gasps]
-Trust me.

665
00:43:50,294 --> 00:43:51,837
Listen, I won't let you down.

666
00:43:52,713 --> 00:43:53,714
Please.

667
00:43:54,965 --> 00:43:55,966
Hey.

668
00:43:57,635 --> 00:43:58,802
[frustrated sigh]

669
00:44:03,515 --> 00:44:05,517
[breath trembling]

670
00:44:21,408 --> 00:44:23,118
[mumbling] You motherfucking fuck.

671
00:44:23,202 --> 00:44:25,412
You fucking piece of shit, motherfucker.

672
00:44:28,082 --> 00:44:30,084
What? What's your deal, huh?

673
00:44:31,168 --> 00:44:32,670
Why do you keep on staring at me?

674
00:44:34,713 --> 00:44:35,714
What?

675
00:44:36,423 --> 00:44:38,300
You think that it's my fault
we're still here?

676
00:44:38,384 --> 00:44:40,219
That it's all because of what I did?

677
00:44:41,679 --> 00:44:43,305
We couldn't have won, Gi-hun.

678
00:44:44,014 --> 00:44:45,808
And it was stupid to ever think we could.

679
00:44:48,102 --> 00:44:49,436
-God damn it!
-[box thuds]

680
00:44:49,520 --> 00:44:52,648
Will you quit looking at me like that?!
This is not my fault!

681
00:44:54,650 --> 00:44:58,445
Listen, we should've gone after
those bastards who hit the "O" button,

682
00:44:58,529 --> 00:45:00,322
then we would've had a chance.

683
00:45:00,406 --> 00:45:02,741
We could've won the fight.
We could've won the vote!

684
00:45:03,826 --> 00:45:05,119
This is your fault.

685
00:45:05,661 --> 00:45:08,622
You and your ridiculous plan,
that's why everybody else is dead.

686
00:45:08,705 --> 00:45:11,834
This is all your fault!
You're the one who got them all killed!

687
00:45:13,210 --> 00:45:14,461
[breathing heavily]

688
00:45:20,050 --> 00:45:22,052
[solemn music]

689
00:45:22,636 --> 00:45:25,472
[woman on PA] Attention.
The game will begin momentarily.

690
00:45:26,765 --> 00:45:30,060
All players on the Blue Team,
please get ready.

691
00:45:30,144 --> 00:45:32,271
You'll be entering the arena first.

692
00:45:32,938 --> 00:45:34,690
Let me repeat the announcement.

693
00:45:35,566 --> 00:45:37,860
The game will begin momentarily.

694
00:45:44,950 --> 00:45:47,035
[Captain] What happened to Woo-seok?
He's not coming?

695
00:45:48,745 --> 00:45:50,956
He called me
just before we left the docks.

696
00:45:51,039 --> 00:45:52,624
Said he had a family emergency.

697
00:45:53,584 --> 00:45:54,418
All of a sudden?

698
00:45:55,794 --> 00:45:58,839
-[scoffs] Guess so.
-Maybe he got scared and bolted.

699
00:45:59,423 --> 00:46:00,549
You know, that's the thing,

700
00:46:00,632 --> 00:46:03,343
guys like him
who always act so tough and talk so loud,

701
00:46:03,427 --> 00:46:05,345
they're a bunch of cowards in the end.

702
00:46:06,763 --> 00:46:08,223
I see it as a good thing.

703
00:46:08,891 --> 00:46:11,435
All he ever did
was drown himself in booze, anyway.

704
00:46:12,144 --> 00:46:14,146
[solemn music]

705
00:46:40,547 --> 00:46:42,925
Mom, please, find a good spot to hide.

706
00:46:43,509 --> 00:46:46,220
I'll just get it over with,
and come find you.

707
00:46:46,303 --> 00:46:49,181
All right?
I'll stay with you and I'll keep you safe.

708
00:46:50,432 --> 00:46:52,518
Yong-sik, I'll be okay.

709
00:46:52,601 --> 00:46:56,271
I mean, think how often your dad
threatened to kill me when he was drunk.

710
00:46:56,355 --> 00:46:58,899
In the end,
which one of your parents died first?

711
00:47:00,108 --> 00:47:01,109
Dad did.

712
00:47:02,528 --> 00:47:04,571
So you really think I'm gonna die here?

713
00:47:05,781 --> 00:47:08,575
[whispering] Besides,
I have my secret weapon.

714
00:47:09,576 --> 00:47:11,119
And I'll use it if I have to.

715
00:47:12,329 --> 00:47:14,748
So don't worry, I'll be just fine.

716
00:47:15,749 --> 00:47:17,501
You focus on making it through.

717
00:47:19,211 --> 00:47:21,338
Whatever it takes,
whatever you need to do,

718
00:47:22,297 --> 00:47:25,175
so we can leave this place together. Huh?

719
00:47:25,759 --> 00:47:26,760
[chuckles]

720
00:47:40,941 --> 00:47:42,067
Swear on your life.

721
00:47:56,456 --> 00:47:57,791
I swear I'll find you.

722
00:48:05,257 --> 00:48:07,259
-[eerie music]
-[players gasp, murmur]

723
00:48:27,487 --> 00:48:28,655
[man] Where do we go?

724
00:48:31,074 --> 00:48:33,160
-[door thuds]
-[players gasp]

725
00:48:33,243 --> 00:48:35,579
-[timer beeps]
-[woman on PA] You now have two minutes.

726
00:48:35,662 --> 00:48:38,582
I repeat, two minutes
until the Red Team enters the arena.

727
00:48:39,124 --> 00:48:41,960
Hey, hey, hey, hey. Everyone.
We should all spread out.

728
00:48:42,044 --> 00:48:44,671
And don't just try to hide.
We need to look for the exit.

729
00:48:44,755 --> 00:48:47,549
Once someone finds a way out of here,
they should shout it out.

730
00:48:47,633 --> 00:48:49,134
So that way, we can all come to them.

731
00:48:49,217 --> 00:48:51,720
Good. Yeah, that's a good plan.
Yeah, if we just work together,

732
00:48:51,803 --> 00:48:53,597
then we can all get out of here
in one piece.

733
00:48:53,680 --> 00:48:56,224
[child's voice on PA]
♪ Hide, hide, it's time to play ♪

734
00:48:56,308 --> 00:48:58,894
-♪ Don't let your hair give you away ♪
-[players clamoring]

735
00:48:59,478 --> 00:49:05,067
♪ Hide, hide, it's time to play
Don't let your clothes give you away ♪

736
00:49:05,150 --> 00:49:10,530
♪ Hide, hide, it's time to play
Don't let your toe give you away ♪

737
00:49:10,614 --> 00:49:15,285
♪ Hide, hide, it's time to play
Don't let your hair give you away ♪

738
00:49:15,369 --> 00:49:16,495
Wanna work together?

739
00:49:17,037 --> 00:49:18,121
What?

740
00:49:18,205 --> 00:49:20,499
-[Nam-gyu chuckles softly]
-[tense music]

741
00:49:20,582 --> 00:49:22,042
Think they'll just let us kill them?

742
00:49:22,626 --> 00:49:24,711
Come on now, use your head. 'Course not.

743
00:49:25,462 --> 00:49:27,381
They'll come at us
with everything they have,

744
00:49:27,464 --> 00:49:29,675
which means,
if we work as a team in there,

745
